  "findings": [
    "Gait tasks with a loaded plate reproduce the authors' strides exactly: normal_walk 1,590 of 1,595 windows matched (the 5 missed contain missing force in our stride), dynamic_walk 747 of 749, incline_walk 744 of 744, walk_backward 572 of 572, weighted_walk 166 of 166, all with 0 ms start offset.",
    "Stairs: 136 of 343 matched (0 ms). 207 missed because each authors' window is one plate contact whose end is not the same leg's next contact; our heel-to-heel rule has no following contact and lists the contact as excluded (248 such contacts). The authors' stairs windows are therefore not heel-to-heel strides.",
    "The five AB01 stair descents without authors' windows give zero strides from our rule (one contact per plate). The plan expected strides there; it does not hold.",
    "side_shuffle: the README's heel-strike rule does not reproduce the authors' windows (5 of 300 matched).",
    "Window tasks: starts agree within the 250 ms tolerance for 60 to 87 percent of windows in jump, lift_weight, lunges, sit_to_stand, squats, step_ups and tire_run (median offset 45 to 110 ms, ours later; ball_toss 45 percent, turn_and_step 54 percent), but ends differ by about 1 s (ours earlier) in squats, lunges, sit_to_stand and lift_weight, because the speed rule splits one authors' window (down plus up) into two spans. Curb and cutting agree poorly (curb_down 1 of 270, curb_up 18 of 258, cutting 36 of 496 matched). Left and right authors' windows are identical in these tasks, so counts repeat per leg.",
    "Tolerances and parameters were fixed before the run; no value was adjusted after seeing the agreement.",
    "For window-rule recordings the missed reason 'no_record_for_this_leg' means our rule found no span in the recording (squats 10); wording only, not rerun.",
